    details = <
        ["de"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::de]>
            purpose = <"Zur Darstellung von Details zu einer physischen Probe, die von einer Person zum Zwecke der Untersuchung, Kontrolle oder Analyse entnommen wurde oder sich auf eine Person bezieht.">
            keywords = <"Probe", "Labor", "Laborprobe", "Entnahme", "Probenahme", "Biopsie", "Gewebe", "Zytologie", "Mikrobiologie", "Pathologie", "Histopathologie", "Histologie", "Laboratorium", "Flüssigkeit", "Abstrich", "Blut", "Exsudat", "Serum", "Plasma", "Urin", "Speichel", "Sekretion", "synovial", "Lymphe", "Kot", "Stuhl", "Exkremente", "Aszites", "Auswurf", "Tupfer", "Muttermilch", "Eiter", "Drainageflüssigkeit", "Knochenmark", "Kultur", "Ausschabung", "Aspirat", "Aderlass", "Test", "zerebrospinale Flüssigkeit", "Pleuraflüssigkeit", "Resektion", "Exzision">
            use = <"Zur Darstellung von Details zu einer physischen Probe, die von einer Person zum Zwecke der Untersuchung, Kontrolle oder Analyse entnommen wurde oder sich auf eine Person bezieht.

Dieser Archetyp wurde speziell für die Verwendung in den folgenden Anwendungsfällen entwickelt: 
- innerhalb von INSTRUCTION.service_request oder einem anderen laborbezogenen INSTRUCTION-Archetyp, um eine zu entnehmende Probe zu beschreiben, oder um eine Probe zu beschreiben, die einer Labordienstleistungsanforderung beigefügt ist;
- innerhalb eines laborbezogenen ACTION-Archetyps zur Beschreibung der Probenentnahme oder einer entnommenen Probe; oder
- innerhalb von OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result oder anderen OBSERVATION-Archetypen im Laborbericht, um die berichtete Probe zu beschreiben.
Darüber hinaus kann dieser Archetyp auch in andere ENTRY- oder CLUSTER-Archetypen eingebettet werden, wenn dies klinisch angemessen ist. 

Der Detaillierungsgrad dieses Archetyps wird wahrscheinlich den derzeit in den meisten Labors erfassten Levels übersteigen. Es wurde bewusst für eine einfache einzelne Probeentnahme konzipiert, gleichzeitige Entnahme mehrerer Proben mit einer einzigen Anforderung und komplexe Situationen, in denen es erforderlich ist, kleinste Details über die Verarbeitung und Aufteilung einer einzelnen Probe darzustellen.

Die genaue Semantik mehrerer Elemente dieses Archetyps, kann sich, basierend auf dem vom Container-Archetyp bereitgestellten Kontext, ändern. Beispielsweise ist das Element \"Methode der Probenentnahme\" im Kontext eines INSTRUCTION-Archetyps die angeforderte Entnahmemethode, während das gleiche Element im Kontext eines ACTION-Archetyps im Status \"Abgeschlossen\" die tatsächliche Entnahmemethode ist.

Dieser Archetyp soll mit anderen CLUSTER-Archetypen wie \"Probenbehälter\", \"Probenverarbeitung\" und „Probentransport“ ergänzt werden.

Dieser Archetyp kann zusammen mit dem Archetyp \"Probenbehälter\" auf zwei Arten verwendet werden: 
- \"Probenbehälter\" verschachtelt in \"Probe\" (z.B. wenn eine venöse Blutprobe in zwei Röhrchen aufgeteilt wird oder ein ganzer Dickdarm in drei Behälter aufgeteilt wird); oder 
- \"Probe\" in \"Probenbehälter\" verschachtelt (z.B. wenn ein Eimer mit Formalin einen Abschnitt des Dickdarms und ein Rektum enthält oder ein Gefäß fünf einzeln markierte Muttermale enthält).

Der Begriff \"Entnahme\" (EN: collection), das in diesem Archetyp verwendet wird, bezieht sich immer auf die Aktivität, die Probe von einer Person zu erhalten. Er soll nicht den Transport der Probe von der Person zum Testlabor darstellen.">
            misuse = <"Nicht zur Erfassung von Informationen über Proben, die sich nicht auf eine bestimmte Person beziehen. Zum Beispiel für routinemäßige Wasserproben aus einem Wasserwerk oder für Stichproben aus Einrichtungen der Lebensmittelproduktion.">
        >
        ["sv"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::sv]>
            purpose = <"Att registrera detaljer om ett provmaterial som tagits från, eller är relaterat till, en individ för undersökning eller analys.">
            keywords = <"provmaterial", "laboratorium", "prov", "provtagning", "biopsi", "vävnad", "kroppsvävnad", "vävnadsprov", "cytologi", "mikobiologi", "patologi", "histopatologi", "histologi", "labb", "vätska", "utstryk", "blod", "exudat", "serum", "plasma", "urin", "saliv", "sekret", "ledvätska", "cysta", "lymfa", "avföring", "faeces", "ascites", "upphostningar", "svabb", "sekret", "kompress", "bröstmjölk", "pus", "var", "dränagevätska", "benmärg", "mikroorganism", "odling", "skrapning", "aspirat", "test", "cerebrospinalvätska", "pleuravätska", "resektion", "excision">
            use = <"Används för att registrera detaljer om ett provmaterial som tagits från, eller är relaterat till, en individ för undersökning eller analys.

Denna CLUSTER-arketyp är utformad för användning i kontexterna som beskrivs nedan:
- Inom INSTRUCTION.service_request eller annan laboratorierelaterad INSTRUCTION-arketyp för att beskriva ett provmaterial som ska tas eller för att beskriva ett provmaterial som åtföljer en begäran om laboratorietjänst.
- Inom en laboratorierelaterad ACTION-arketyp för att beskriva en provtagning **ALTERNATIV: insamling av ett provmaterial** eller ett provtaget material.
- Inom OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result eller annan laboratorierelaterad OBSERVATION-arketyp för att beskriva det provmaterial som ett laboratorieresultat bygger på.
Dessutom kan arketypen också nästlas i andra ENTRY- eller CLUSTER-arketyper, där det är kliniskt lämpligt.

Detaljnivån i denna arketyp är sannolikt högre än vad som för närvarande registreras i de flesta laboratorier. Den är avsiktligt utformad för att stödja både enkel provtagning av ett enskilt prov, samtidig provtagning av flera prov vid en och samma beställning, samt mer komplexa situationer där mycket detaljerad information om hur ett prov förbereds och delas upp behöver dokumenteras.

De specifika betydelserna för flera datafält i den här arketypen kan variera beroende på sammanhanget i den överordnade arketyp där denna arketyp är nästlad. Till exempel kommer datafältet \"Provtagningsmetod\" i kontexten för en INSTRUCTION-arketyp avse den planerade provtagningsmetoden, medan samma datafält i kontexten för en ACTION-arketyp med status \"completed\" avse den metod som faktiskt användes.

Denna arketyp kompletteras av andra CLUSTER-arketyper med detaljer om \"Specimen container\", \"Specimen preparation\" och \"Transport of an item\".

Denna arketyp har utformats för att användas med arketypen ”Specimen container” på två huvudsakliga sätt:
- ”Specimen container” nästlad i ”Specimen” (till exempel när ett venöst blodprov är uppdelat mellan två rör eller om en hel tjocktarm är uppdelad i tre hinkar) eller
- \"Specimen\" nästlad i \" Specimen container\" (till exempel när en hink med formalin innehåller en sektion av tjocktarmen och en sektion av rektumet).

OBS! Termen \"provtagning\" i denna arketyp är avsedd att betyda aktiviteten för att samla in provmaterial från en individ. Det är inte avsett att representera transporten av ett provmaterial från en individ till laboratoriet.
">
            misuse = <"Ska inte användas för att registrera information om provmaterial som inte är relaterat till en specifik patient, såsom exempelvis rutinprover från vattenverk eller slumpmässiga prover från livsmedelsproduktion.">
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
            purpose = <"For å registrere detaljer om et fysisk prøvemateriale tatt fra eller relatert til et individ, for undersøkelse eller analyse.">
            keywords = <"laboratorium", "prøve", "prøvetaking", "laboratorieprøve", "prøvemateriale", "prøveeksemplar", "preparat", "prøvesamling", "biopsi", "vevsprøve", "celleprøve", "mikrobiologi", "patologi", "histologi", "lab", "væske", "utstryk", "blod", "sårvæske", "serum", "plasma", "urin", "spytt", "sekret,", "leddvæske", "lymfe", "avføring", "ascites", "ekspektorat", "pensel", "morsmelk", "puss", "drensvæske", "beinmarg", "kultur", "avskrap", "aspirat">
            use = <"Brukes for å registrere detaljer om et fysisk prøvemateriale tatt fra eller relatert til et individ, for undersøkelse eller analyse.

Denne CLUSTER-arketypen er laget for å brukes i de tre hovedsammenhengene beskrevet under:
- Innenfor INSTRUCTION.service_request eller en annen laboratorierelatert INSTRUCTION-arketype for å beskrive et prøvemateriale som skal tas, eller for å beskrive prøvematerialet som ligger ved en laboratorierekvisisjon.
- Innenfor en laboratorierelatert ACTION-arketype for å beskrive prøvetaking eller et prøvemateriale som er tatt
- Innenfor OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result eller en annen laboratorierelatert OBSERVATION-arketype for å beskrive prøvematerialet som ligger til grunn for et laboratorieresultat.
I tillegg kan arketypen også brukes innenfor andre ENTRY- eller CLUSTER-arketyper, der det er klinisk passende.

Det er sannsynlig at detaljnivået i denne arketypen overgår nåværende dataregistrering i de fleste laboratorier. Den er ment for å være brukbar både for en enkel prøvetaking, samtidig innhenting av flere prøvematerialer med én rekvisisjon, og komplekse situasjoner det det må registreres mye detaljer om preparering og oppdeling av et prøvemateriale.

De spesifikke betydningene av flere elementer i denne arketypen vil endre seg ut fra den overordnede arketypen som Prøvemateriale-arketypen settes inn i. For eksempel vil elementet \"Prøvetakingsmetode\" i kontekst av en INSTRUCTION-arketype være den rekvirerte prøvetakingsmetoden, mens det samme elementet i kontekst av en ACTION-arketype i tilstanden \"completed\" være den faktiske prøvetakingsmetoden som ble brukt.

Denne arketypen kompletteres av andre CLUSTER-arketyper for konsepter som Prøvebeholder, Prøvepreparering, og transport og lagring av prøvemateriale.

Denne arketypen kan brukes sammen med Prøvebeholder-arketypen på to hovedmåter:
- Ved nøsting av \"Prøvebeholder\" inni \"Prøvemateriale\" (for eksempel når et vakuumglass med venøst blod fordeles på to mindre glass, eller en hel tykktarm deles på tre bøtter)
- Med \"Prøvemateriale\" nøstet inni \"Prøvebeholder\" (for eksempel når en bøtte inneholder en seksjon av en tykktarm og en endetarm, eller et glass inneholder fem individuelt merkede føflekker)

NB! Uttrykket \"prøvetaking\" er i denne arketypen ment å bety aktiviteten å ta en prøve fra et individ. Det er ikke ment å representere transporten fra individet til laboratoriet.">
            misuse = <"Ikke ment å brukes til å registrere informasjon om prøvemateriale som ikke er relaterte til et spesifikt individ, som for eksempel rutineprøver fra vannverk eller stikkprøver fra matvareproduksjon.">
        >
        ["pt-br"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::pt-br]>
            purpose = <"Para gravar detalhes de um espécime laboratorial. Será frequentemente usado em diferentes contextos, p.e, dentro de um arquétipo tipo Instruction para descrever os espécimes que devem ser obtidos, ou descrevendo o espécime que acompanha a solicitação laboratorial. Pode ocorre dentro de um arquétipo tipo Action, p.e., descrevendo espécimes retirados como parte de um procedimento cirúrgico. 

Será finalmente utilizado dentro de um arquétipo de resultado laboratorial para descrever o espécime reportado.">
            keywords = <"*specimen (en)", "*laboratory (en)", "*sample (en)", "*collection (en)", "*sampling (en)", "*biopsy (en)", "*tissue (en)", "*cytology (en)", "*microbiology (en)", "*pathology (en)", "*histopathology (en)", "*histology (en)", "*lab (en)", "*fluid (en)", "*smear (en)", "*blood (en)", "*exudate (en)", "*serum (en)", "*plasma (en)", "*urine (en)", "*saliva (en)", "*secretion (en)", "*synovial (en)", "*lymph (en)", "*feces (en)", "*faeces (en)", "*fæces (en)", "*ascites (en)", "*expectorate (en)", "*swab (en)", "*breast milk (en)", "*pus (en)", "*drain fluid (en)", "*bone marrow (en)", "*culture (en)", "*scraping (en)", "*aspirate (en)", "*phlebotomy (en)", "*test (en)", "*cerebrospinal fluid (en)", "*pleural fluid (en)", "*resection (en)", "*excision (en)">
            use = <"Geralmente utilizado dentro de OBSERVATION. laboratory_test.v1 e outros arquétipos tipo Instruction ou Action relacionados.">
            misuse = <"">
        >
        ["en"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
            purpose = <"To record details about a physical sample collected from, or related to, an individual for the purpose of investigation, examination or analysis.">
            keywords = <"specimen", "laboratory", "sample", "collection", "sampling", "biopsy", "tissue", "cytology", "microbiology", "pathology", "histopathology", "histology", "lab", "fluid", "smear", "blood", "exudate", "serum", "plasma", "urine", "saliva", "secretion", "synovial", "lymph", "feces", "faeces", "fæces", "ascites", "expectorate", "swab", "breast milk", "pus", "drain fluid", "bone marrow", "culture", "scraping", "aspirate", "phlebotomy", "test", "cerebrospinal fluid", "pleural fluid", "resection", "excision">
            use = <"Use to record details about a physical sample collected from, or related to, an individual for the purpose of investigation, examination or analysis.

This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the following use cases:
- within INSTRUCTION.service_request or another laboratory-related INSTRUCTION archetype to describe a specimen that is to be collected, or to describe a specimen that accompanies a laboratory service request; 
- within a laboratory-related ACTION archetype to describe specimen collection or a specimen that has been collected; or
- within OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result or other laboratory reporting OBSERVATION archetypes to describe the specimen being reported.
In addition this archetype can also be nested within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes, where clinically appropriate.

The level of detail in this archetype is likely to exceed that currently collected in most laboratories. It has deliberately been designed to cater for a simple, single specimen collection; simultaneous collection of multiple specimens with a single request; and complex situations where it is required to record minute detail about the preparation and subdivision of a single specimen.

The exact semantics of several elements of this archetype may change based on the context provided by the parent archetype in which it is nested. For example, the 'Collection method' element in the context of an INSTRUCTION archetype is the requested collection method, while the same element in the context of an ACTION archetype in the 'completed' state is the actual collection method.

Other complementary archetypes will carry the detail about 'Specimen container', 'Specimen preparation', and 'Specimen transport'.

This archetype has been designed to be used with the Specimen container archetype in two main ways: 
- 'Specimen container' nested within 'Specimen' (for example when a venous blood specimen is divided between two vials, or a whole large intestine is divided into three buckets); or
- 'Specimen' nested within 'Specimen container' (for example when a bucket of formalin contains a section of large intestine and a rectum, or a jar contains five individually marked moles).

Please note: The term 'collection' used in this archetype always refers to the activity of obtaining a specimen from an individual. It is not intended to represent the transport of the specimen from the individual to the testing laboratory.">
            misuse = <"Not intended to be used for recording information about specimens that are not related to a specific individual. For example routine water samples from a waterworks, or spot samples from food production facilities.">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["ar-sy"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::ar-sy]>
            purpose = <"لتسجيل تفاصيل حول عينة بالمعمل. 
يستخدم غالبا في سياقات مختلفة, مثلا: في داخل نموذج (تعليمات) ليصف العينة التي ينبغي أخذها, أو يصف العينة المرافقة لطلب معملي. 
و قد يحدث ذلك في داخل نموذج (فعل), مثال: وصف العينات التي تم أخذها كجزء من إجراء طبي جراحي. 
و سيستخدم أخيرا في داخل نموذج نتيجة اختبار المعمل ليصف العينة التي يتم تقديم عينة حولها.">
            keywords = <"*specimen (en)", "*laboratory (en)", "*sample (en)", "*collection (en)", "*sampling (en)", "*biopsy (en)", "*tissue (en)", "*cytology (en)", "*microbiology (en)", "*pathology (en)", "*histopathology (en)", "*histology (en)", "*lab (en)", "*fluid (en)", "*smear (en)", "*blood (en)", "*exudate (en)", "*serum (en)", "*plasma (en)", "*urine (en)", "*saliva (en)", "*secretion (en)", "*synovial (en)", "*lymph (en)", "*feces (en)", "*faeces (en)", "*fæces (en)", "*ascites (en)", "*expectorate (en)", "*swab (en)", "*breast milk (en)", "*pus (en)", "*drain fluid (en)", "*bone marrow (en)", "*culture (en)", "*scraping (en)", "*aspirate (en)", "*phlebotomy (en)", "*test (en)", "*cerebrospinal fluid (en)", "*pleural fluid (en)", "*resection (en)", "*excision (en)">
            use = <"يستخدم عادةً في داخل نموذج (ملاحظة. معمل) و النماذج الأخرى تعليمات و فعل المتعلقة بالمعمل.">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
        >
        ["fr"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::fr]>
            purpose = <"Pour enregistrer les informations relatives à un échantillon physique prélevé sur une personne ou lié à celle-ci à des fins d'enquête, d'examen ou d'analyse.">
            keywords = <"échantillon", "laboratoire", "prélèvement", "biopsie", "tissu", "cytologie", "microbiologie", "pathologie", "histopathologie", "histologie", "lab", "liquide", "frottis", "sang", "exsudat", "sérum", "plasma", "urine", "salive", "sécrétion", "synovial", "lymph", "matières fécales", "ascite", "expectoration", "écouvillon", "lait maternel", "pus", "liquide de drainage", "moelle osseuse", "culture", "prélèvement par raclage", "aspirat", "phlébotomie", "test", "liquide céphalo-rachidien", "liquide pleural", "résection", "excision">
            use = <"À utiliser pour enregistrer les détails relatifs à un échantillon physique prélevé sur une personne ou lié à celle-ci à des fins d’investigation, d’examen ou d’analyse.

Cet archétype a été spécialement conçu pour être utilisé dans les cas d’utilisation suivants :
- au sein de INSTRUCTION.service_request ou d’un autre archétype INSTRUCTION lié à un laboratoire, pour décrire un échantillon devant être prélevé, ou pour décrire un échantillon accompagnant une demande de service de laboratoire ; 
- au sein d’un archétype ACTION lié à un laboratoire pour décrire le prélèvement d’un échantillon ou un échantillon qui a été prélevé ; ou
- au sein d’OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result ou d’autres archétypes OBSERVATION relatifs aux rapports de laboratoire pour décrire l’échantillon faisant l’objet du rapport.
De plus, cet archétype peut également être imbriqué dans d’autres archétypes ENTRY ou CLUSTER, lorsque cela est cliniquement approprié.

Le niveau de détail de cet archétype est susceptible de dépasser celui actuellement recueilli dans la plupart des laboratoires. Il a été délibérément conçu pour prendre en charge un prélèvement simple et unique d’un échantillon ; le prélèvement simultané de plusieurs échantillons dans le cadre d’une seule demande ; ainsi que des situations complexes où il est nécessaire d’enregistrer les moindres détails concernant la préparation et la subdivision d’un seul échantillon.

La sémantique exacte de plusieurs éléments de cet archétype peut varier en fonction du contexte fourni par l’archétype parent dans lequel il est imbriqué. Par exemple, l’élément « Méthode de prélèvement » dans le contexte d’un archétype INSTRUCTION correspond à la méthode de prélèvement demandée, tandis que ce même élément, dans le contexte d’un archétype ACTION à l’état « terminé », correspond à la méthode de prélèvement effective.

D’autres archétypes complémentaires fourniront les détails concernant le « Récipient pour échantillons », la « Préparation de l’échantillon » et le « Transport de l’échantillon ».

Cet archétype a été conçu pour être utilisé avec l’archétype « Specimen container » de deux manières principales : 
- « Récipient pour échantillons » imbriqué dans « Échantillon » (par exemple lorsqu’un échantillon de sang veineux est réparti entre deux flacons, ou qu’un gros intestin entier est divisé en trois seaux) ; ou
- « Échantillon » imbriqué dans « Récipient pour échantillons » (par exemple lorsqu’un seau de formol contient une section du gros intestin et un rectum, ou qu’un bocal contient cinq grains de beauté marqués individuellement).

Remarque : le terme « prélèvement » utilisé dans cet archétype fait toujours référence à l’activité consistant à prélever un échantillon sur une personne. Il n’est pas destiné à désigner le transport de l’échantillon de la personne vers le laboratoire d’analyse.">
            misuse = <"À ne pas utiliser pour enregistrer des informations concernant des échantillons qui ne sont pas liés à une personne spécifique. Par exemple, des prélèvements d’eau de routine effectués dans une station de traitement d’eau ou des prélèvements ponctuels effectués dans des installations de production alimentaire.">
        >
        ["ca"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::ca]>
            purpose = <"Registrar detalls sobre una mostra física recollida a un pacient o relacionada amb ell, amb finalitats de recerca, examen o anàlisi.">
            keywords = <"mostra", "laboratori", "recollida", "mostreig", "biòpsia", "teixit", "citologia", "microbiologia", "patologia", "histopatologia", "histologia", "laboratori", "líquid", "frotis", "sang", "exsudat", "sèrum", "plasma", "orina", "saliva", "secreció", "sinovial", "limfa", "excrements", "excrements", "ascitis", "expectorar", "hisop", "llet materna", "pus", "drenar líquid", "medul·la òssia", "cultura", "raspat", "aspirar", "flebotomia", "prova", "líquid cefaloraquidi", "líquid pleural", "resecció", "excissió">
            use = <"S'utilitza per registrar detalls sobre una mostra física recollida a un pacient o relacionada amb ell, amb finalitats de recerca, examen o anàlisi.

Aquest arquetip ha estat dissenyat específicament per utilitzar-se en els casos d'ús següents:
- dins d'INSTRUCTION.service_request o un altre arquetip de tipus INSTRUCTION relacionat amb el laboratori, per descriure una mostra que s'ha de recollir o per descriure una mostra que acompanya una petició de laboratori;
- dins un arquetip de tipus ACTION relacionat amb el laboratori per descriure la recollida de mostres o una mostra que s'ha recollit; o
- dins d'OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result o altres arquetips de tipus OBSERVATION d'informes de laboratori per descriure la mostra que se n'informa.
A més, aquest arquetip també es pot niar dins d'altres arquetips de tipus ENTRY o CLUSTER, quan sigui clínicament apropiat.

És probable que el nivell de detall d'aquest arquetip superi el que es recull actualment a la majoria dels laboratoris. Ha estat dissenyat a propòsit per atendre una recollida simple d'una sola mostra; recollida simultània de múltiples mostres amb una sola sol·licitud; i situacions complexes en què cal registrar detalls minuciosos sobre la preparació i subdivisió d'una sola mostra.

La semàntica d'alguns elements d'aquest arquetip pot canviar segons el context proporcionat per l'arquetip principal al qual estigui imbricat. Per exemple, l'element 'Mètode de recollida' dins el context d'un arquetip de tipus INSTRUCTION és el mètode de recollida sol·licitat, mentre que el mateix element dins el context d'un arquetip de tipus ACTION a l'estat 'completat' és el mètode de recollida real.

Altres arquetips complementaris inclouran detalls sobre \"Contenidor de mostres\", \"Preparació de mostres\" i \"Transport de mostres\".

Aquest arquetip ha estat dissenyat per utilitzar-se juntament amb l'arquetip de contenidor de mostres de dues maneres principals:
- 'Contenidor de mostra' imbricat dins de 'Mostra' (per exemple, quan una mostra de sang venosa es divideix en dos vials o una mostra de l'intestí gruixut es divideix en tres pots); o
- 'Mostra' imbricada dins de 'Contenidor de mostra' (per exemple, quan un pot de formaldehid conté una secció d'intestí gruixut i un recte, o un flascó conté cinc mostres cutànies marcades individualment).

Cal tenir en compte: el terme \"recollida\" utilitzat en aquest arquetip sempre fa referència a l'activitat d'obtenir una mostra d'un individu. No vol representar el transport de la mostra des de l'individu fins al laboratori de proves.">
            misuse = <"No està destinat a ser utilitzat per registrar informació sobre mostres que no estiguin relacionades amb un pacient concret. Per exemple, mostres d'aigua d'una planta d'abastament d'aigua o mostres puntuals d'instal·lacions de producció d'aliments.">
        >
        ["es"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::es]>
            purpose = <"Registrar detalles sobre una muestra física recogida a un paciente o relacionada con él, con fines de investigación, examen o análisis.">
            keywords = <"muestra", "laboratorio", "recogida", "muestreo", "biopsia", "tejido", "citología", "microbiología", "patología", "histopatología", "histología", "laboratorio", "líquido", "frotis", "sangre", "exudado", "suero", "plasma", "orina", "saliva", "secreción", "sinovial", "linfa", "heces", "excrementos", "ascitis", "expectorar", "hisopo", "leche materna", "pus", "drenar liquido", "médula ósea", "cultura", "raspado", "aspirar", "flebotomía", "prueba", "líquido cefalorraquídeo", "líquido pleural", "resección", "excisión">
            use = <"Se utiliza para registrar detalles sobre una muestra física recogida a un paciente o relacionada con él, con fines de investigación, examen o análisis.

Este arquetipo ha sido diseñado específicamente para usarse en los siguientes casos de uso:
- dentro de INSTRUCTION.service_request u otro arquetipo de tipo INSTRUCTION relacionado con el laboratorio, para describir una muestra que se va a recoger o para describir una muestra que acompaña a una petición de laboratorio;
- dentro de un arquetipo de tipo ACTION relacionado con el laboratorio para describir la recogida de muestras o una muestra que se ha recogido; o
- dentro de OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result u otros arquetipos de tipo OBSERVATION de informes de laboratorio para describir la muestra que se informa.
Además, este arquetipo también puede anidarse dentro de otros arquetipos de tipo ENTRY o CLUSTER, cuando sea clínicamente apropiado.

Es probable que el nivel de detalle de este arquetipo supere el que se recoge actualmente en la mayoría de los laboratorios. Ha sido diseñado a propósito para atender una recogida simple de una sola muestra; recogida simultánea de múltiples muestras con una sola solicitud; y situaciones complejas en las que es necesario registrar detalles minuciosos sobre la preparación y subdivisión de una sola muestra.

La semántica de algunos elementos de este arquetipo puede cambiar según el contexto proporcionado por el arquetipo principal al que esté anidado. Por ejemplo, el elemento 'Método de recogida' dentro del contexto de un arquetipo de tipo INSTRUCTION, es el método de recogida solicitado, mientras que el mismo elemento dentro del contexto de un arquetipo de tipo ACTION en el estado 'completado', es el método de recogida real.

Otros arquetipos complementarios incluirán detalles sobre \"Contenedor de muestras\", \"Preparación de muestras\" y \"Transporte de muestras\".

Este arquetipo ha sido diseñado para usarse junto con el arquetipo de contenedor de muestras de dos maneras principales:
- 'Contenedor de muestra' anidado dentro de 'Muestra' (por ejemplo, cuando una muestra de sangre venosa se divide en dos viales o una muestra del intestino grueso se divide en tres botes); o
- 'Muestra' anidada dentro de 'Contenedor de muestra' (por ejemplo, cuando un bote de formaldehído contiene una sección de intestino grueso y un recto, o un frasco contiene cinco muestras cutáneas marcadas individualmente).

A tener en cuenta: el término \"recogida\" utilizado en este arquetipo siempre se refiere a la actividad de obtener una muestra de un individuo. No pretende representar el transporte de la muestra desde el individuo hasta el laboratorio de pruebas.">
            misuse = <"No está destinado a ser utilizado para registrar información sobre muestras que no estén relacionadas con un paciente en concreto. Por ejemplo, muestras de agua de una planta de abastecimiento de agua o muestras puntuales de instalaciones de producción de alimentos.">
        >
    >

definition
    CLUSTER[id1] matches {    -- Specimen
        items cardinality matches {1..*; unordered} matches {
            ELEMENT[id30] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Specimen type
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9002]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id99] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Specimen label
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9003]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id98] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Specimen description
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9004]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id100] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Number of fragments
                value matches {
                    DV_COUNT[id9005]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id2] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Laboratory specimen identifier
                value matches {
                    DV_IDENTIFIER[id9006]
                    DV_TEXT[id9007]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id89] matches {    -- External identifier
                value matches {
                    DV_IDENTIFIER[id9008]
                    DV_TEXT[id9009]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id35] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Date/time received
                value matches {
                    DV_DATE_TIME[id9010]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id9] matches {    -- Sampling context
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9011]
                }
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id28] matches {    -- Physical properties
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.specimen_measurements(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.inspection_body_fluid(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v0\..*/}
            }
            ELEMENT[id8] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Collection method
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9012]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id80] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Collection description
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9013]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id88] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Source site
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9014]
                }
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id14] matches {    -- Structured source site
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.anatomical_location(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.anatomical_location_circle(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.anatomical_location_relative(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v2\..*/}
            }
            ELEMENT[id16] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Collection date/time
                value matches {
                    DV_DATE_TIME[id9015]
                    DV_INTERVAL<DV_DATE_TIME>[id9016]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id6] matches {    -- Hazard warning
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9017]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id68] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Collection setting
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9018]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id71] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Specimen collector identifier
                value matches {
                    DV_IDENTIFIER[id9019]
                    DV_TEXT[id9020]
                }
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id72] matches {    -- Specimen collector details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.person(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.organisation(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*/}
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id84] matches {    -- Additional details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/.*/}
            }
            ELEMENT[id81] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Number of containers
                value matches {
                    DV_COUNT[id9021] matches {
                        magnitude matches {|>=0|}
                    }
                }
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id86] matches {    -- Container details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.specimen_container(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*/}
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id69] matches {    -- Processing details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.specimen_preparation(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.specimen_preparation(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v0\..*/}
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id101] matches {    -- Storage details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.biobank_storage(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v0\..*|openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.biobank_storage(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*/}
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id94] matches {    -- Transport details
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.specimen_transport(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*/}
            }
            allow_archetype CLUSTER[id97] matches {    -- Digital representation
                include
                    archetype_id/value matches {/openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER\.media_file(-[a-zA-Z0-9_]+)*\.v1\..*/}
            }
            ELEMENT[id4] matches {    -- Parent specimen identifier
                value matches {
                    DV_IDENTIFIER[id9022]
                    DV_TEXT[id9023]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id43] matches {    -- Specimen quality issue
                value matches {
                    DV_CODED_TEXT[id9024] matches {
                        defining_code matches {[ac9000]}    -- Specimen quality issue (synthesised)
                    }
                    DV_TEXT[id9025]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id42] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Adequacy for testing
                value matches {
                    DV_CODED_TEXT[id9026] matches {
                        defining_code matches {[ac9001]}    -- Adequacy for testing (synthesised)
                    }
                    DV_TEXT[id9027]
                }
            }
            ELEMENT[id46] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Comment
                value matches {
                    DV_TEXT[id9028]
                }
            }
        }
    }

terminology
    term_definitions = <
        ["de"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"Probe">
                description = <"Eine physikalische Probe zur Prüfung, Untersuchung oder Analyse, die von einer Person entnommen wurde oder die sich auf die Person bezieht.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Gewebe oder Körperflüssigkeit.">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"Laborprobenidentifikator">
                description = <"Eine eindeutige Kennung der Probe, die normalerweise vom Labor vergeben wird.">
                comment = <"Wird manchmal als \"Accession Identifier\" bezeichnet. Probenbehälter, z. B. Vakuumröhrchen oder Gewebekassetten, haben ihre eigenen Kennungen, die im Element \"Behälter-Identifikator\" des Archetyps \"Probenbehälter\" eingetragen werden können.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.accessionIdentifier">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"Identifikator der übergeordneten Probe">
                description = <"Eindeutige Kennung der übergeordneten Probe(n), wobei die Probe in Teilproben aufgeteilt wird.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: eine bestimmte Probe eines Objektträgers für die Histologie würde einen bestimmten Paraffinwachsblock als Ausgangsprobe haben.">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"Gefahrenhinweis">
                description = <"Jegliches Risiko oder jede Biogefährdung für den Probenehmer oder das Laborpersonal aufgrund der Exposition gegenüber oder Kontakt mit der Probe.
">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: \"Hepatitis B\"; \"Nervenmittel\". Die Codierung des \"Gefahrenhinweises\" mit einer Terminologie wird, wenn möglich, bevorzugt.">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"Probenentnahmemethode">
                description = <"Die Methode der Probenentnahme, die angewendet wird oder wurde.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Venenpunktion, Biopsie, Resektion. Nach Möglichkeit wird die Codierung der Probenentnahmemethode mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt. Wenn die Probenentnahmemethode über vorkoordinierte Codes in das Element \"Probenart\" einbezogen wird, wird dieses Datenelement überflüssig.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.method">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"Probenentahmebedingung">
                description = <"Der Kontext, in dem die Probe entnommen wird.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: \"Fasten\", \"volle Blase\", \"steriles Feld\" oder spezielle Anweisungen zur Handhabung oder sofortigen Verarbeitung der Probe, zum Beispiel \"Nach Erhalt zentrifugieren\". Kann auch verwendet werden, um bekannte Abweichungen von Entnahme- oder Handhabungsanweisungen zu dokumentieren, z.B. dass der Patient nicht gefastet hat. Wenn möglich, wird eine Kodierung der Probenentahmebedingung mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt. 

Ob dieses Element Bedingungen enthält, die während der Probeentnahme vorhanden sein sollten oder waren, hängt vom Kontext des Container-Archetyps ab, in der Regel ein INSTRUCTION-Archetyp. Der Inhalt dieses Elements im Kontext eines ACTION-Archetyps in einem abgeschlossenen Zustand kann verwendet werden, um zu entscheiden, ob signifikante Störfaktoren im Zusammenhang mit der Entnahme aufgetreten sind, die zum einpflegen des Elements \"Störfaktoren\" des Archetyps OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result verwendet werden können.">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"Probenentnahmestelle strukturiert">
                description = <"Strukturierte Angaben zur Körperstelle, an der die Probe entnommen wurde.">
                comment = <"Verwenden Sie diesen Archetypen zur Beschreibung strukturierter oder komplexerer anatomischen Stellen oder zur Unterstützung der Darstellung der Entnahmestelle während der Anwendung. Wenn die Körperstelle über vorab koordinierte Codes in das Element \"Probenentnahmestelle\" einbezogen wird, wird die Verwendung dieses SLOTs überflüssig.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.bodySite">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"Zeitpunkt der Probenentnahme">
                description = <"Das Datum und die Uhrzeit, zu der die Probennahme angeordnet wurde oder stattfand.">
                comment = <"Dieser Zeitpunkt wird hauptsächlich in den Zeitangaben, von INSTRUCTION, ACTION oder OBSERVATION erfasst. Da es sich jedoch um eine wichtige Information handelt, kann es nützlich sein, diese auch direkt mit der Probe selbst zu verknüpfen.">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"Physikalische Eigenschaften">
                description = <"Physikalische Größen, Masse oder nicht messbare Eigenschaften der Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Volumen, Masse, Umfang, Farbe, Geruch, Trübung. Mit diesem Element können die Eigenschaften der zu entnehmenden Probe im Kontext eines INSTRUCTION-Archetyps oder die Eigenschaften der zu entnehmenden Probe im Kontext eines ACTION- oder OBSERVATION-Archetyps angegeben werden. Beispielsweise kann eine INSTRUCTION die Entnahme von 20 ml Blut verlangen, während die entsprechende ACTION aufzeichnet, dass nur 15 ml entnommen wurden.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.quantity">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"Probenart">
                description = <"Die Art der Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Venöses Blut, Bakterienkultur, Zytologie oder Gewebeprobe. Nach Möglichkeit wird die Codierung der Probenart mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.type">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"Zeitpunkt des Probeneingangs">
                description = <"Datum und Uhrzeit des Eingangs der Probe im Labor.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.receivedTime">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"Eignung zur Analyse">
                description = <"Angabe darüber, ob die Probe für die Untersuchung geeignet war.">
                comment = <"Dieses Element soll verwendet werden, um zu beurteilen, ob die Probenqualität für die Prüfung ausreichend war oder nicht und ob eine Prüfung durchgeführt wurde oder nicht. Die Codierung der Eignung zum Testen mit einer Terminologie wird nach Möglichkeit bevorzugt.">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"Qualitätsmangel der Probe">
                description = <"Ein bestimmter Qualitätsmangel einer Probe.">
                comment = <"Die Codierung des Qualitätsmangels der Probe mit einer Terminologie, wird nach Möglichkeit bevorzugt.">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"Kommentar">
                description = <"Zusätzliche Beschreibungen der Probe, die nicht in anderen Feldern abgebildet werden können.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.note">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"Hämolysiert">
                description = <"Die Probe war hämolysiert.">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"Lipämisch">
                description = <"Die Probe war lipämisch.">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"Falsches Additiv">
                description = <"Der Probe wurde ein falsches Additiv wie Transportmedium oder Konservierungsmittel zugesetzt.">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"Unzureichende Menge">
                description = <"Die zur Verfügung stehende Probenmenge reichte nicht aus, um die Untersuchung durchzuführen.">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"Zufriedenstellend">
                description = <"Die Probe ist von ausreichender Qualität, um eine Berichterstattung zu ermöglichen.">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"Mangelhaft - analysiert">
                description = <"Die Probe ist mangelhaft, wurde aber analysiert.">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"Mangelhaft - nicht analysiert">
                description = <"Die Probe ist mangelhaft und wurde nicht analysiert.">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"Umgebung der Probenentnahme">
                description = <"Identifizierung der physikalischen Umgebung, in der die Probe entnommen wird.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Laborambulanz, zu Hause oder Krankenhausstation. Dies gibt den Ort der Probenentnahme im Gesundheitswesen an. Auf diese Weise kann das Labor bei Bedarf Fragen zur Entnahme der Probe stellen. Die Vorgabe zur Probenentnahme kann zusätzliche Informationen enthalten, die für die Analyse des Ergebnisses relevant sind.">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"Angaben zur Verarbeitung">
                description = <"Strukturierte Angaben zur Vorbereitung oder Verarbeitung der Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Färbung oder Fixierung.">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"Identifikator des Probenehmers">
                description = <"Identifizierung der für die Entnahme der Probe verantwortliche Person oder Organisation.">
                comment = <"Dieses Element soll verwendet werden, wenn die Probe bereits entnommen wurde und der tatsächliche Probenehmer bekannt ist.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.collector">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"Angaben zum Probenehmer">
                description = <"Die für die Entnahme der Probe verantwortliche Person oder Organisation.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.collector">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"Beschreibung der Entnahme">
                description = <"Beschreibung der Probenentnahme.">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"Anzahl der Behälter">
                description = <"Die Gesamtzahl der physischen Einheiten, in denen sich die Probe befindet.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: Anzahl der Behälter, Gefäße, Fläschchen, Röhrchen, Blöcke, Objektträger oder Gitter.">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"Zusätzliche Angaben">
                description = <"Zusätzliche strukturierte Angaben zu der Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel Details zu Nadelbiopsien bei Prostatakrebs, bei denen sowohl die Anforderung als auch die Beschreibung über die Probe detailliert und spezifisch sind.">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"Behälter Details">
                description = <"Details über Behälter, der/die verwendet wurde/n.">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"Probenentnahmestelle">
                description = <"Identifizierung der Körperstelle oder einer anderen Stelle, an der die Probe entnommen wird.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: „Wunde an linker Wade“, „IV-Kanüle rechter Arm“, „rechte Niere“. 
Nach Möglichkeit wird die Codierung des Namens der Probenentnahmestelle mit einer Terminologie bevorzugt. Verwenden Sie dieses Datenelement, um vorkoordinierte Probenentnahmestellen zu erfassen. Wenn die Anforderungen für die Darstellung der Probenentnahmestelle zur Laufzeit der Anwendung bestimmt werden oder diese eine komplexere Modellierung erfordern, z.B. relative Positionen, verwenden Sie in diesem Archetyp den SLOT \"Probenentnahmestelle strukturiert\". Wenn die Probenentnahmestelle über vorab koordinierte Kodes in das Element \"Probenart\" einbezogen wird, wird dieses Datenelement überflüssig.">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"Externer Identifikator">
                description = <"Eine eindeutige Kennung der Probe, die von einer Organisation außerhalb des Labors wie dem Auftraggeber zugeordnet wurde.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: \"Anforderer-ID\", \"Archiv-ID\", \"Biobank-ID\".">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.identifier">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"Ikterisch">
                description = <"Die Probe war ikterisch.">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"Verarbeitungsfehler">
                description = <"Beim Umgang mit der Probe ist ein Fehler aufgetreten. Zum Beispiel: Falsche Lagerung, zerbrochener Behälter.">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"Alter">
                description = <"Die Probe war zu alt, um sie akkurat zu analysieren.">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"Technischer Fehler">
                description = <"Die Probe konnte aus technischen Gründen nicht analysiert werden.">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"Angaben zum Transport">
                description = <"Strukturierte Angaben zum Transport der Probe.">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"Geronnen">
                description = <"Die Probe war geronnen.">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"Falsch beschriftet">
                description = <"Das Probe war falsch beschriftet.">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"Digitale Darstellung">
                description = <"Strukturierte Details über eine digitale Darstellung der Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel das gescannte Bild eines Histopathologie-Dias.">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"Beschreibung der Probe">
                description = <"Beschreibung der untersuchten Probe.">
                comment = <"Zum Beispiel: die Farbe und Viskosität einer Flüssigkeit, die Form eines festen Gewebes oder eine Beschreibung von Gewebefragmenten.">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"Probenbezeichnung">
                description = <"Ein Name oder Label, der/das die Probe beschreibt.">
                comment = <"Normalerweise nur für anatomisch-pathologische Proben relevant. Zum Beispiel: „Sigmoidresektion mit einem Stück Blasenwand“ oder „Aggregat mehrerer Hautbiopsiefragmente“.">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"Anzahl der Fragmente">
                description = <"Die Anzahl der Gewebeteilen, aus denen die Probe besteht.">
                comment = <"Normalerweise nur relevant, wenn mehrere Gewebefragmente untersucht und als einzelne Probe berichtet werden.">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"Angaben zur Lagerung">
                description = <"Strukturierte Angaben zur Probenaufbewahrung.">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"Qualitätsmangel der Probe (synthesised)">
                description = <"Ein bestimmter Qualitätsmangel einer Probe. (synthesised)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"Eignung zur Analyse (synthesised)">
                description = <"Angabe darüber, ob die Probe für die Untersuchung geeignet war. (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["sv"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"Provmaterial">
                description = <"Ett provmaterial taget från, eller relaterat till, en individ i syfte att utföra en bedömning, undersökning eller analys.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis vävnad eller kroppsvätska.">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"Laboritoriets providentifierare">
                description = <"En unik providentifierare för provmaterialet, vanligen angiven av laboratoriet.">
                comment = <"Syftet är identifiering av ett provmaterial i ett laboratorieinformationssystem. Provbehållare såsom exempelvis vakuumflaskor och vävnadskassetter har sina egna ID-nummer vilka kan anges i datafältet \"Container ID\" i arketypen CLUSTER.specimen_container.

">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"Ursprungsprovets identifierare">
                description = <"Unik identifierare för ursprungsprovet, där provmaterialet har delats upp i delprover.">
                comment = <"Till exempel: Ett specifikt objektglas inom histologi kan ha ett specifikt paraffinvaxblock som sitt ursprungsprov.
">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"Riskvarning">
                description = <"Identifierad hälsofara eller biologisk fara för provtagaren eller laboratoriepersonalen vid exponering för eller kontakt med provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Till exempel \"hepatit B\" eller \"nervmedel\". Kodning av riskvarning med en terminologi är att föredra, där det är möjligt.
">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"Provtagningsmetod">
                description = <"Den metod som används för att ta provet.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis venpunktion, biopsi eller resektion. Kodning av provtagningsmetod till en terminologi är att föredra i de fall det är möjligt. Om provtagningsmetoden inkluderas i \"Provtyp\" via prekoordinerade koder blir detta datafält överflödigt. 
">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"Provtagningskontext">
                description = <"Den kontext i vilken provet togs.">
                comment = <"Exempel: fastande, full urinblåsa, sterilt fält. Alternativt specialinstruktioner avseende hanteringen av provmaterialet eller omedelbar beredning av provmaterialet såsom \"centrifugera vid mottagande\". Det här datafältet kan även användas för att dokumentera olika typer av kända avvikelser vid provtagning eller instruktioner kring hantering såsom exempelvis att patienten inte hade fastat trots att det uttryckligen hade begärts. Kodning av provtagningskontexten till en terminologi är att föredra i de fall det är möjligt. 

Om arketypen är nästlad i en INSTRUCTION-arketyp kommer kontexten att återspegla de avsedda eller önskade förhållandena för provtagningen.

Om arketypen används för att representera ett steg i en ACTION-arketyp som härrör till att provtagningen utförs eller slutförs kommer kontexten att återspegla de förhållanden som fanns vid provtagningen och detta kan även kopieras till datafältet \"Möjliga felkällor\" i arketypen OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result.
">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"Strukturerad provkälla">
                description = <"En beskrivning av den strukturerade anatomiska positionen från vilken provet togs.">
                comment = <"Använd de mer detaljerade arketyperna för att beskriva strukturerade eller mer komplexa anatomiska positioner, eller för att stödja applikationen för att upptäcka positionen. Om den anatomiska platsen ingår i \"Provkälla\" via förkoordinerade koder blir denna SLOT överflödig.
">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"Datum/tid för provtagning">
                description = <"Datum och tid för när provtagningen ska äga rum eller har ägt rum.">
                comment = <"Datum/tid kommer främst att anges i arketyper av typerna INSTRUCTION, ACTION eller OBSERVATION. Detta är dock en kritisk informationsdel och därför det kan vara användbart att ha möjlighet att också länka den direkt till provmaterialet.

">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"Fysiska egenskaper">
                description = <"Provmaterialets fysiska dimensioner, massa eller icke mätbara egenskaper.">
                comment = <"Till exempel: Volym, massa, omkrets, färg, lukt eller turbiditet (grumlighet). Detta datafält kan nästlas i en INSTRUCTION-arketyp för att specificera egenskaperna hos ett provmaterial som ska samlas in, alternativt i en ACTION-arketyp eller OBSERVATION-arketyp för att ange egenskaper hos ett provmaterial som redan har samlats in. Till exempel kan en INSTRUCTION-arketyp begära att 20 mL blod ska samlas in, medan motsvarande ACTION-arketyp registrerar att 15 mL blod insamlades.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.quantity">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"Provtyp ELLER Typ av provmaterial">
                description = <"Typ av provmaterial">
                comment = <"Exempelvis venöst blod, bakteriekultur, cytologi eller vävnadsprov. Kodning av provtypen till en terminologi är att föredra i de fall det är möjligt.">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"Datum/tid ankomst">
                description = <"Datum och tid när provmaterialet togs emot av laboratoriet.">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"Analysbarhet">
                description = <"Information om huruvida provmaterialet var av tillräcklig kvalitet för analys.">
                comment = <"Detta datafält är avsett för att registrera ett beslut om huruvida kvaliteten av provmaterialet var tillräckligt bra för att genomföra en analys och om analysen har genomförts. Kodning av analysbarheten till en terminologi är att föredra där det är möjligt.">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"Provkvalitetsproblem">
                description = <"Ett specifikt kvalitetsproblem med provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Kodning av kvalitetsproblem till en terminologi är att föredra i de fall det är möjligt.">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"Kommentar">
                description = <"Ytterligare fritext om provmaterialet som inte omfattas av andra datafält.">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"Hemolyserat">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var hemolyserat.">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"Lipemiskt">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var lipemiskt.">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"Felaktigt additiv">
                description = <"Ett felaktigt tillsatsmedel, såsom ett transportmedium eller konserveringsmedel, tillsattes till provmaterialet.">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"Otillräcklig mängd">
                description = <"Den tillgängliga mängden provmaterial var otillräcklig för att genomföra undersökningen.">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"Tillfredställande">
                description = <"Provmaterialet är av tillfredsställande kvalitet.">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"Otillfredsställande - behandlat">
                description = <"Provmaterialet är av otillfredsställande kvalitet men har analyserats.">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"Otillfredsställande - ej behandlat">
                description = <"Provmaterialet är av otillfredsställande kvalitet och har inte analyserats.">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"Provtagningsmiljö">
                description = <"Den fysiska miljö i vilken provmaterialet samlades in.">
                comment = <"Till exempel: Laboratoriets öppenvårdsmottagning, hemma eller sjukhusavdelning. Detta datafält specificerar i vilken typ av miljö provmaterialet samlades in. Provtagningssituationen kan också ge ytterligare information som är relevant för tolkningen av resultatet.
">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"Information om bearbetning">
                description = <"Strukturerade detaljer om beredning eller bearbetning av provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Till exempel: fixering eller färgning.">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"Provtagaridentifierare">
                description = <"Identifierare av den person eller organisation som ansvarar för provtagningen.">
                comment = <"Detta datafältet är avsett att användas när provmaterialet redan har samlats in och den faktiska provtagaren är känd.">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"Detaljer om provtagaren">
                description = <"Den person eller organisation som ansvarar för provtagningen.">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"Beskrivning av provtagning">
                description = <"Fritextbeskrivning av provtagningen.">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"Antal provbehållare">
                description = <"Det totala antalet enheter som provmaterialet är distribuerat i. 
">
                comment = <"Till exempel: antal provbehållare, provrör, provflaskor, block, objektglas eller galler.

">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"Ytterligare detaljer">
                description = <"Ytterligare strukturerade detaljer om provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis: detaljer om mellannålsbiopsier vid prostatacancer, där både beställning och svarsrapportering om provmaterialet är detaljerade och specifika.">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"Detaljer om provbehållare">
                description = <"Detaljer om provbehållare som har använts.">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"Provkälla">
                description = <"Identifiering av den anatomiska positionen eller annat ställe som provet är taget från.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis \"sår på vänster underben\", \"venkateter på höger arm\", \"höger njure\". Kodning av provkälla till en terminologi är att föredra i de fall det är möjligt.

Använd detta datafält för att ange prekoordinerade provkällor. Om behoven för registrering av den anatomiska positionen kan genereras automatiskt av vissa IT-system eller kräver komplex modellering såsom relativa platser, använd SLOT \"Strukturerad anatomisk position\" i denna arketyp. Om den anatomiska positionen ingår i \"Provtyp\" via förkoordinerade koder blir detta datafält överflödigt.
">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"Extern identifierare">
                description = <"En unik identifierare för provmaterial som anges av en extern part utanför laboratoriet.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis remiss-ID, beställnings-ID, arkiverings-ID, Biobank-ID.">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"Ikteriskt">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var ikteriskt.">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"Hanteringsfel">
                description = <"Ett fel inträffade vid hantering av provmaterialet. Till exempel: Felaktig lagring eller trasig behållare.">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"Ålder">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var för gammalt för att analysera eller för att analysera korrekt.">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"Tekniskt fel">
                description = <"Provmaterialet kunde inte analyseras på grund av tekniska skäl.">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"Transportdetaljer">
                description = <"Strukturerade detaljer om transport av provmaterialet.">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"Koagulerat">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var koagulerat.">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"Felaktig märkning">
                description = <"Provmaterialet var felaktigt märkt.">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"Digital representation">
                description = <"Strukturerade detaljer om digital representation av provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Till exempel den inskannade bilden av ett histopatologiskt objektglas.">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"Beskrivning av provmaterial ELLER Provbeskrivning">
                description = <"Beskrivning av det provmaterial som undersöks.">
                comment = <"Till exempel: färgen och viskositeten hos en vätska; formen av en fast vävnad; eller en beskrivning av vävnadsfragment.
">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"Provmaterialets benämning">
                description = <"Namn eller etikett som beskriver provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Vanligtvis endast relevant för anatomiska patologiprover. Till exempel: 'resektion av sigmoideum med en bit av blåsväggen' eller 'aggregering av flera hudbiopsifragment'.">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"Antal fragment">
                description = <"Antal vävnadsfragment som ingår i provmaterialet.">
                comment = <"Vanligtvis endast relevant när ett antal vävnadsfragment undersöks tillsammans och rapporteras gemensamt som ett enda provmaterial.">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"Lagringsdetaljer">
                description = <"Strukturerade detaljer om förvaringen av provmaterialet.">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"Provkvalitetsproblem (synthesised)">
                description = <"Ett specifikt kvalitetsproblem med provmaterialet. (synthesised)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"Analysbarhet (synthesised)">
                description = <"Information om huruvida provmaterialet var av tillräcklig kvalitet för analys. (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"Prøvemateriale">
                description = <"Et fysisk prøvemateriale tatt fra eller relatert til et individ, for undersøkelse eller analyse.">
                comment = <"For eksempel kroppsvev eller kroppsvæske.">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"Laboratoriets identifikator">
                description = <"En unik identifikator av prøvematerialet, som regel tilordnet av laboratoriet.">
                comment = <"I noen sammenhenger, som HL7 og IHE, kalt \"Accession Identifier\", mens et norsk synonym er \"Prøvenummer\". Prøvebeholdere, for eksempel vakuumglass eller vevskassetter, har egne IDer som registreres i elementet \"BeholderID\" i arketypen Prøvebeholder.">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"Identifikator av overordnet prøve">
                description = <"Unik identifikator for den overordnede prøven, i de tilfeller der prøven deles inn i flere del-prøver.">
                comment = <"For eksempel kan et spesifikt prøveglass med et histologisnitt ha en spesifikk blokk med parafinvoks som sin overordnede prøve.">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"Risikovarsel">
                description = <"Identifisert helserisiko eller biologisk risiko for prøvetakeren eller laboratoriepersonell ved eksponering for eller kontakt med prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel \"Hepatitt B\" eller \"nervegift\". Koding av Risikovarsel med en terminologi er foretrukket, der det er mulig.">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"Prøvetakingsmetode">
                description = <"Prøvetakingsmetoden som er brukt.">
                comment = <"For eksempel venepunksjon, biopsi eller reseksjon. Koding av prøvetakingsmetoden med en terminologi er foretrukket, når det er mulig. Dersom prøvetakingsmetoden er inkludert i \"Type prøvemateriale\" gjennom bruk av prekoordinerte koder blir dette elementet overflødig.">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"Prøvetakingsforhold">
                description = <"Forhold under prøvetaking.">
                comment = <"For eksempel \"fastende\", \"full blære\", \"sterilt felt\" eller en hvilken som helst instruksjon om håndtering eller umiddelbar prosessering av prøvematerialet, for eksempel \"sentrifugeres umiddelbart etter mottak\". Dette dataelementet kan også brukes for å dokumentere kjente avvik fra prøvetakings- eller håndteringsinstruksjoner, for eksempel at pasienten ikke var fastende til tross for at dette var forordnet. Koding av prøvetakingsforholdene med en terminologi foretrekkes, der det er mulig.

Hvis denne arketypen brukes innenfor en INSTRUCTION-arketype, vil dette elementet reflektere ønskede eller forordnede forhold ved prøvetakingen. Hvis arketypen brukes innenfor en ACTION-arketype et prosesstrinn som medfører at prøvetakingen er under uføring eller er utført, vil dette elementet reflektere forhold som faktisk var tilstede ved prøvetakingen. Dette kan også kopieres til elementet \"Konfunderende faktorer\" i arketypen OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result.">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"Strukturert anatomisk lokalisering">
                description = <"En strukturert anatomisk lokalisering der prøvematerialet ble tatt fra.">
                comment = <"Bruk de mer detaljerte arketypene for å beskrive strukturerte eller mer komplekse anatomiske steder, eller for å støtte at applikasjonen kan registrere lokaliseringen. Dersom den anatomiske lokaliseringen er med i \"Type prøvemateriale\" via prekoordinerte koder, blir dette SLOTet overflødig.">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"Dato/tid for prøvetaking">
                description = <"Dato og tid for når prøvetakingen skal skje, eller har skjedd.">
                comment = <"Denne dato/tidsregistreringen vil primært registreres i forbindelse med INSTRUCTION-timing, ACTION-tid, eller OBSERVATION-tider. Imidlertid er dette en kritisk informasjonsbit, og det kan være nyttig å ha mulighet til å også knytte den direkte til prøvematerialet.">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"Fysiske egenskaper">
                description = <"Fysiske dimensjoner, masse eller ikke-målbare egenskaper ved prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel volum, masse, omkrets, farge, lukt, turbiditet. Dette elementet kan brukes for å angi egenskapene ved prøvematerialet som skal innhentes, i konteksten av en INSTRUCTION-arketype, eller egenskapene ved prøvematerialet som ble innhentet, i konteksten av en ACTION- eller OBSERVATION-arketype. For eksempel kan det i en INSTRUCTION bestilles innhenting av 20 ml blod, mens det i den korresponderende ACTION-arketypen registreres at bare 15 ml ble innhentet.">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"Type prøvemateriale">
                description = <"Type prøvemateriale.">
                comment = <"For eksempel venøst blod, bakteriekultur, celleprøve eller vevsprøve. Koding av prøvetypen med en terminologi er foretrukket, dersom mulig.">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"Dato/tid for mottak">
                description = <"Datoen og klokkeslettet da prøven ble mottatt på laboratoriet.">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"Analyserbarhet">
                description = <"Informasjon om hvorvidt prøvematerialet var av tilstrekkelig kvalitet for analyse.">
                comment = <"Dette elementet er ment for å registrere en avgjørelse om hvorvidt prøvematerialet var av god nok kvalitet for analyse, og om analysen er gjennomført. Koding av analyserbarheten med en terminologi er foretrukket der det er mulig.">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"Kvalitetsproblem">
                description = <"Et spesifikt problem med kvaliteten på prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"Koding av kvalitetsproblemet med en terminologi foretrekkes der det er mulig.">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"Kommentar">
                description = <"Ytterligere fritekst om prøvematerialet som ikke dekkes av andre felt.">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"Hemolysert">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet var hemolysert.">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"Lipemisk">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet var lipemisk.">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"Feil tilsetningsstoff">
                description = <"Det er brukt feil tilsetningsstoff, transportmedium, fikseringmedium eller prøverør.">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"Utilstrekkelig mengde">
                description = <"Ikke nok prøvemateriale til analysering.">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"Tilfredstillende">
                description = <"Prøven er av tilfredsstillende kvalitet.">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"Utilfredstillende - behandlet">
                description = <"Prøven har/er av utilfredsstillende kvalitet, men har blitt analysert.">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"Utilfredstillende - ikke behandlet">
                description = <"Prøven har utilfredsstillende kvalitet og har ikke blitt analysert.">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"Prøvetakingsomgivelser">
                description = <"Den fysiske situasjonen der prøvematerialet ble innhentet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel laboratorieprøvemottak, i hjemmet, eller sengepost. Dette elementet spesifiserer typen omgivelser prøvematerialet ble tatt i. Prøvetakingssituasjonen kan også gi ytterligere informasjon som er relevant for tolkningen av resultatet.">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"Prosesseringsdetaljer">
                description = <"Strukturerte detaljer om preparering eller prosessering av prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel farging eller fiksering.">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"Prøvetakers ID">
                description = <"Identifikator for personen eller organisasjonen som er ansvarlig for prøvetakingen.">
                comment = <"Dette elementet er ment brukt der prøvematerialet allerede er innhentet, og den faktiske prøvetakeren er kjent.">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"Detaljer om prøvetaker">
                description = <"Personen eller organisasjonen som er ansvarlig for prøvetakingen.">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"Beskrivelse av prøvetaking">
                description = <"Fritekstbeskrivelse av prøvetakingen. Dette elementet kalles i noen sammenhenger også \"Prøvetakers kommentar\".">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"Antall beholdere">
                description = <"Det totale antallet fysiske enheter som prøvematerialet er fordelt på.">
                comment = <"For eksempel antall bøtter, glass, rør, mikrorør, blokker, prøveglass eller grid.">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"Ytterligere detaljer">
                description = <"Ytterligere strukturerte detaljer om prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel detaljer om nålebiopsier ved prostatakreft, der både rekvisisjonen og svarrapporten inneholder mange spesifikke detaljer om prøvematerialet.">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"Detaljer om beholder">
                description = <"Detaljer om brukte beholdere.">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"Opprinnelsessted">
                description = <"Kroppssted eller annen lokalisering som prøven er tatt fra.">
                comment = <"For eksempel \"sår på venstre legg\", \"venekateter på høyre arm\", \"høyre nyre\".
Koding av den anatomiske lokaliseringen med en terminologi er foretrukket der det er mulig. Bruk dette dataelementet til å registrere prekoordinerte anatomiske lokaliseringer. Dersom behovene for registrering av den anatomiske lokaliseringen bestemmes i applikasjonen eller krever kompleks modellering slik som relative lokaliseringer, bruk SLOTet \"Strukturert anatomisk lokalisering\" i denne arketypen. Dersom den anatomiske lokaliseringen er med i \"Type prøvemateriale\" via prekoordinerte koder, blir dette dataelementet overflødig.">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"Ekstern identifikator">
                description = <"En unik identifikator av prøvematerialet, tilordnet av en part utenfor laboratoriet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel \"Rekvirentens ID\", \"ArkivID\" eller \"BiobankID\".">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"Ikterisk">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet var ikterisk.">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"Håndteringsfeil">
                description = <"En feil oppsto ved håndtering av prøven. For eksempel feil oppbevaring, knust prøveglass.">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"Alder">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet var for gammelt til å analyseres eller analyseres nøyaktig.">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"Teknisk feil">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet kunne ikke analyseres av tekniske årsaker.">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"Transportdetaljer">
                description = <"Strukturerte detaljer om transport av prøvematerialet.">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"Koagulert">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet var koagulert.">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"Feilmerking">
                description = <"Prøvematerialet ble feilmerket.">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"Digital representasjon">
                description = <"Strukturerte detaljer om en digital representasjon av prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"For eksempel et scannet bilde av et prøveglass innen patologi.">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"Prøvemateriale beskrivelse">
                description = <"Fritekstbeskrivelse av prøvematerialet som blir undersøkt.">
                comment = <"For eksempel: fargen og viskositeten til en væske; formen til et solid vev; eller en beskrivelse av vevsfragmenter.">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"Prøvemateriale navn">
                description = <"Et navn eller etikett som beskriver prøvematerialet.">
                comment = <"Vanligvis kun relevant for anatomiske patologiprøver. For eksempel: 'Sigmoidreseksjon med et stykke blærevegg' eller 'Aggregat av flere hudbiopsifragmenter'">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"Antall fragmenter">
                description = <"Antall vevsfragmenter prøvemateriale består av.">
                comment = <"Vanligvis bare relevant når en rekke vevsfragmenter undersøkes og rapporteres som en enkelt prøve.">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"Lagringsdetaljer">
                description = <"Strukturerte detaljer om arkivering/lagring av prøvematerialet.">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"Kvalitetsproblem (synthesised)">
                description = <"Et spesifikt problem med kvaliteten på prøvematerialet. (synthesised)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"Analyserbarhet (synthesised)">
                description = <"Informasjon om hvorvidt prøvematerialet var av tilstrekkelig kvalitet for analyse. (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["pt-br"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"Espécime">
                description = <"*A specimen collected from an individual or related to that individual. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Tissue, body fluid or food. (en)">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"Identificador laboratorial do espécime">
                description = <"*A unique identifier of the specimen, normally assigned by the laboratory. (en)">
                comment = <"*Sometimes called the Accession Identifier. Specimen containers, for example vacuum vials or tissue cassettes, have their own identitiers which may be recorded in the 'Container identifier' element in the 'Specimen container' archetype. (en)">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"Identificador de origem do espécime">
                description = <"Identificador único do espécime original, onde o espécime é dividido em sub-amostras.">
                comment = <"*For example: A specific histology slide specimen would have a specific paraffin wax block as its parent specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"*Hazard warning (en)">
                description = <"*Identified health risk or biohazard to the collector or laboratory staff due to exposure to, or contact with, the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: 'Hepatitis B'; \"nerve agent'. Coding of the 'Hazard warning' with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"Método de coleta">
                description = <"*The method of collection used. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: venepuncture, biopsy, resection. Coding of the collection method with a terminology is preferred, where possible. If the collection method is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant. (en)">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"*Sampling context (en)">
                description = <"*A condition that should be or was present when the sample is to be or was taken. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: 'fasting'; 'full bladder'; 'sterile field'; or special instructions on the handling or immediate processing of the sample, such as 'centrifuge on receipt'. This data element also be used to document any known deviations from collection or handling instructions, for example that the patient had not fasted, even when this had been originally requested. Coding of the 'Sampling context' with a terminology is preferred, where possible.

If this archetype is used within an INSTRUCTION archetype, the context will reflect the intended or desired conditions at sample collection. If this archetype is used for representing an ACTION archetype pathway step which correlates with the collection being performed or completed, the context will be reflecting the conditions that existed at sample collection and this may also be copied to the 'Confounding factors' element of the OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result archetype. (en)">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"*Structured source site (en)">
                description = <"*A structured description of the area of the body from where the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*Utilise the more detailed archetypes to describe structured or more complex anatomical sites, or to support recording the source site at run-time by the application. If the body site has been fully identified in the 'Source site' data element, this SLOT becomes redundant. (en)">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"*Collection date/time (en)">
                description = <"A data e horário em que a coleta foi solicitada ou realizada.">
                comment = <"*This datetime will be captured primarily in the INSTRUCTION timing, ACTION time or OBSERVATION times. However, as this is a critical piece of information, it can be useful to also associate it directly with the specimen itself. (en)">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"Propriedades físicas">
                description = <"*Physical dimensions, mass or non-measurable properties of the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Volume, mass, circumference, colour, smell, turbidity. This element can be used to specify the properties of the specimen to be collected, in the context of an INSTRUCTION archetype, or the properties of the specimen which was collected, in the context of an ACTION or OBSERVATION archetype. For example, an INSTRUCTION may request the collection of 20 ml of blood, while the corresponding ACTION records that only 15 ml was collected. (en)">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"Tipo de espécime">
                description = <"*The type of specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Venous blood, bacterial culture, cytology, or prostatic biopsy. Coding of the specimen type with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"*Date/time received (en)">
                description = <"A data e horário em que a amostra foi recebida no laboratório.">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"Adequação para teste">
                description = <"*Information about whether the specimen was adequate for testing. (en)">
                comment = <"*This element is intended to be used to record a judgement about whether or not the specimen quality was good enough for testing, and whether or not testing has been carried out. Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen quality issue (en)">
                description = <"*A specific quality issue with a specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"Comentário">
                description = <"*Additional narrative about the specimen not captured in other fields. (en)">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"Hemolisado">
                description = <"O espécime estava hemolisado.">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"Lipêmico">
                description = <"O espécime estava lipêmico.">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"Meio de transporte incorreto">
                description = <"Um preservante incorreto foi usado para transportar o espécime.">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"Amostra insuficiente">
                description = <"Uma amostra insuficiente foi fornecida para realização da medição.">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"Satisfatório">
                description = <"O espécime é de qualidade suficiente para realizar o procedimento.">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"Insatisfatório - processado">
                description = <"O espécime é insatisfatório mais foi processado.">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"Insatisfatório - não processado">
                description = <"O espécime é insatisfatório e não foi processado.">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"Contexto da coleta">
                description = <"*Identification of the physical setting in which the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: laboratory outpatient clinic, at home, or hospital ward. This specifies the type of specimen collection location within the healthcare environment. It enables the laboratory to ask questions about the collection of the specimen, if required. The specimen collection setting may provide additional information relevant to the analysis of the result. (en)">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"Detalhes do processamento">
                description = <"*Details about preparation or processing of the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Staining or fixation. (en)">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"Identificador do coletor do espécime">
                description = <"*Identifier of the person or organisation responsible for collecting the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*This element is intended to be used where the specimen has already been collected and the actual collector is known. (en)">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"Detalhes do coletor do espécime">
                description = <"A pessoa ou organização responsável pela coleta do espécime.">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"*Collection description (en)">
                description = <"*Additional narrative description about the collection of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"Número de recipientes">
                description = <"*The total number of physical units holding this specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Number of buckets, jars, vials, tubes, blocks, slides or grids. (en)">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"*Additional details (en)">
                description = <"*Additional structured details about the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: details about needle biopsies in prostate cancer, where both the request and reporting about the specimen are detailed and specific. (en)">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"Detalhes do recipiente">
                description = <"*Details about containers used. (en)">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"*Source site (en)">
                description = <"*Identification of the body site or other location from where the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*Coding of the name of the source site with a terminology is preferred, where possible. Use this data element to record precoordinated source sites. If the requirements for recording the source site are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the 'Structured source site' SLOT in this archetype. If the source site is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant. (en)">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"*External identifier (en)">
                description = <"*A unique identifier of the specimen, assigned by a party external to the laboratory such as the requester. (en)">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"*Icteric (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was icteric. (en)">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"*Handling error (en)">
                description = <"*An error arose when handling the specimen. For example: The specimen was spilled, or stored outside the recommended temperature range. (en)">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"*Age (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was too old to analyse accurately. (en)">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"*Technical failure (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen could not be analysed for technical reasons. (en)">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"*Transport details (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about transport of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"*Clotted (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was clotted. (en)">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"*Incorrectly labelled (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was labelled incorrectly. (en)">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"*Digital representation (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about a digital representation of the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example the scanned image of a histopathology slide. (en)">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen description (en)">
                description = <"*Narrative description about the specimen being examined. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: the color and viscosity of a liquid; the shape of a solid tissue; or a description of tissue fragments. (en)">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen label (en)">
                description = <"*A name or label describing the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Usually only relevant for anatomical pathology samples. For example: 'Sigmoid resection with a piece of bladder wall' or 'Aggregate of multiple skin biopsy fragments'. (en)">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"*Number of fragments (en)">
                description = <"*The number of tissue fragments comprising the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Usually only relevant when a number of tissue fragments are being examined and reported on as a single specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"*Storage details (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about the storage of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen quality issue (en) (synthesised)">
                description = <"*A specific quality issue with a specimen. (en) (synthesised)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"Adequação para teste (synthesised)">
                description = <"*Information about whether the specimen was adequate for testing. (en) (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["ar-sy"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"العينة">
                description = <"*A specimen collected from an individual or related to that individual. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Tissue, body fluid or food. (en)">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"*Laboratory Specimen Identifier(en)">
                description = <"*A unique identifier of the specimen, normally assigned by the laboratory. (en)">
                comment = <"*Sometimes called the Accession Identifier. Specimen containers, for example vacuum vials or tissue cassettes, have their own identitiers which may be recorded in the 'Container identifier' element in the 'Specimen container' archetype. (en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.accessionIdentifier(en)">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"*Parent Specimen Identifier(en)">
                description = <"*Unique identifier of the parent specimen, where the specimen is split into sub-samples.(en)">
                comment = <"*For example: A specific histology slide specimen would have a specific paraffin wax block as its parent specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"*Hazard warning (en)">
                description = <"*Identified health risk or biohazard to the collector or laboratory staff due to exposure to, or contact with, the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: 'Hepatitis B'; \"nerve agent'. Coding of the 'Hazard warning' with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"*Collection Method(en)">
                description = <"*The method of collection used. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: venepuncture, biopsy, resection. Coding of the collection method with a terminology is preferred, where possible. If the collection method is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant. (en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.collection.method(en)">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"*Sampling context (en)">
                description = <"*A condition that should be or was present when the sample is to be or was taken. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: 'fasting'; 'full bladder'; 'sterile field'; or special instructions on the handling or immediate processing of the sample, such as 'centrifuge on receipt'. This data element also be used to document any known deviations from collection or handling instructions, for example that the patient had not fasted, even when this had been originally requested. Coding of the 'Sampling context' with a terminology is preferred, where possible.

If this archetype is used within an INSTRUCTION archetype, the context will reflect the intended or desired conditions at sample collection. If this archetype is used for representing an ACTION archetype pathway step which correlates with the collection being performed or completed, the context will be reflecting the conditions that existed at sample collection and this may also be copied to the 'Confounding factors' element of the OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result archetype. (en)">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"*Structured source site (en)">
                description = <"*A structured description of the area of the body from where the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*Utilise the more detailed archetypes to describe structured or more complex anatomical sites, or to support recording the source site at run-time by the application. If the body site has been fully identified in the 'Source site' data element, this SLOT becomes redundant. (en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.collection.sourceSite(en)">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"*Collection date/time (en)">
                description = <"*The date and time that collection has been ordered to take place or has taken place.(en)">
                comment = <"*This datetime will be captured primarily in the INSTRUCTION timing, ACTION time or OBSERVATION times. However, as this is a critical piece of information, it can be useful to also associate it directly with the specimen itself. (en)">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"*Physical properties(en)">
                description = <"*Physical dimensions, mass or non-measurable properties of the specimen. (en)">
                fhir_mappings = <"*Specimen.collection.quantity(en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Volume, mass, circumference, colour, smell, turbidity. This element can be used to specify the properties of the specimen to be collected, in the context of an INSTRUCTION archetype, or the properties of the specimen which was collected, in the context of an ACTION or OBSERVATION archetype. For example, an INSTRUCTION may request the collection of 20 ml of blood, while the corresponding ACTION records that only 15 ml was collected. (en)">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen Type(en)">
                description = <"*The type of specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Venous blood, bacterial culture, cytology, or prostatic biopsy. Coding of the specimen type with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.type(en)">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"*Date/time received (en)">
                description = <"*The date and time that the sample was received at the laboratory.(en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.receivedTime(en)">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"المناسبة لإتمام التحليل">
                description = <"*Information about whether the specimen was adequate for testing. (en)">
                comment = <"*This element is intended to be used to record a judgement about whether or not the specimen quality was good enough for testing, and whether or not testing has been carried out. Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen quality issue (en)">
                description = <"*A specific quality issue with a specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible. (en)">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"تعليق">
                description = <"*Additional narrative about the specimen not captured in other fields. (en)">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"تم حل الدم">
                description = <"تم حل الدم في العينة">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"العينة بها فرط شحيمات">
                description = <"العينة بها فرط شحيمات">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"وسط نقل غير صحيح">
                description = <"تم استخدام مادة حافظة غير صحيحة عند نقل العينة">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"عينة غير كافية">
                description = <"تم إعطاء عينة غير كافية لإتمام القياس">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"مُرضِية">
                description = <"العينة بجودة كافية بما يسمح للحصول على تقرير للاختبار">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"غير مُرضية - تمت معالجتها">
                description = <"العينة غير مُرضية و لكن تمت معالجتها">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"غير مُرضية - لم تتم معالجتها">
                description = <"العينة غير مُرضية و لم تتم معالجتها">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"*Collection Setting(en)">
                description = <"*Identification of the physical setting in which the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: laboratory outpatient clinic, at home, or hospital ward. This specifies the type of specimen collection location within the healthcare environment. It enables the laboratory to ask questions about the collection of the specimen, if required. The specimen collection setting may provide additional information relevant to the analysis of the result. (en)">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"*Additional Preparation(en)">
                description = <"*Details about preparation or processing of the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Staining or fixation. (en)">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen Collector Identifier(en)">
                description = <"*Identifier of the person or organisation responsible for collecting the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*This element is intended to be used where the specimen has already been collected and the actual collector is known. (en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.collection.collector(en)">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen Collector Details(en)">
                description = <"*The person or organisation responsible for collecting the specimen.(en)">
                fhir_mapping = <"*Specimen.collection.collector(en)">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"*Collection description (en)">
                description = <"*Additional narrative description about the collection of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"*Number of Containers(en)">
                description = <"*The total number of physical units holding this specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: Number of buckets, jars, vials, tubes, blocks, slides or grids. (en)">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"*Additional details (en)">
                description = <"*Additional structured details about the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: details about needle biopsies in prostate cancer, where both the request and reporting about the specimen are detailed and specific. (en)">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"*Container Details(en)">
                description = <"*Details about containers used. (en)">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"*Source site (en)">
                description = <"*Identification of the body site or other location from where the specimen is collected. (en)">
                comment = <"*Coding of the name of the source site with a terminology is preferred, where possible. Use this data element to record precoordinated source sites. If the requirements for recording the source site are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the 'Structured source site' SLOT in this archetype. If the source site is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant. (en)">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"*External identifier (en)">
                description = <"*A unique identifier of the specimen, assigned by a party external to the laboratory such as the requester. (en)">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"*Icteric (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was icteric. (en)">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"*Handling error (en)">
                description = <"*An error arose when handling the specimen. For example: The specimen was spilled, or stored outside the recommended temperature range. (en)">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"*Age (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was too old to analyse accurately. (en)">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"*Technical failure (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen could not be analysed for technical reasons. (en)">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"*Transport details (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about transport of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"*Clotted (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was clotted. (en)">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"*Incorrectly labelled (en)">
                description = <"*The specimen was labelled incorrectly. (en)">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"*Digital representation (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about a digital representation of the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example the scanned image of a histopathology slide. (en)">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen description (en)">
                description = <"*Narrative description about the specimen being examined. (en)">
                comment = <"*For example: the color and viscosity of a liquid; the shape of a solid tissue; or a description of tissue fragments. (en)">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen label (en)">
                description = <"*A name or label describing the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Usually only relevant for anatomical pathology samples. For example: 'Sigmoid resection with a piece of bladder wall' or 'Aggregate of multiple skin biopsy fragments'. (en)">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"*Number of fragments (en)">
                description = <"*The number of tissue fragments comprising the specimen. (en)">
                comment = <"*Usually only relevant when a number of tissue fragments are being examined and reported on as a single specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"*Storage details (en)">
                description = <"*Structured details about the storage of the specimen. (en)">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"*Specimen quality issue (en) (synthesised)">
                description = <"*A specific quality issue with a specimen. (en) (synthesised)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"المناسبة لإتمام التحليل (synthesised)">
                description = <"*Information about whether the specimen was adequate for testing. (en) (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["en"] = <
            ["id1"] = <
                text = <"Specimen">
                description = <"A physical sample collected from, or related to, an individual for the purpose of investigation, examination or analysis.">
                comment = <"For example: Tissue or body fluid.">
            >
            ["id2"] = <
                text = <"Laboratory specimen identifier">
                description = <"A unique identifier of the specimen, normally assigned by the laboratory.">
                comment = <"Sometimes called the Accession Identifier. Specimen containers, for example vacuum vials or tissue cassettes, have their own identitiers which may be recorded in the 'Container identifier' element in the 'Specimen container' archetype.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.accessionIdentifier">
            >
            ["id4"] = <
                text = <"Parent specimen identifier">
                description = <"Unique identifier of the parent specimen, where the specimen is split into sub-samples.">
                comment = <"For example: A specific histology slide specimen can have a specific paraffin wax block as its parent specimen.">
            >
            ["id6"] = <
                text = <"Hazard warning">
                description = <"Identified health risk or biohazard to the collector or laboratory staff due to exposure to, or contact with, the specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: 'Hepatitis B'; \"nerve agent'. Coding of the 'Hazard warning' with a terminology is preferred, where possible.">
            >
            ["id8"] = <
                text = <"Collection method">
                description = <"The method of collection used.">
                comment = <"For example: venepuncture, biopsy, resection. Coding of the collection method with a terminology is preferred, where possible. If the collection method is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.method">
            >
            ["id9"] = <
                text = <"Sampling context">
                description = <"The context in which the specimen is collected.">
                comment = <"For example: 'fasting'; 'full bladder'; 'sterile field'; or special instructions on the handling or immediate processing of the sample, such as 'centrifuge on receipt'. This data element also be used to document any known deviations from collection or handling instructions, for example that the patient had not fasted, even when this had been originally requested. Coding of the 'Sampling context' with a terminology is preferred, where possible.

If this archetype is used within an INSTRUCTION archetype, the context will reflect the intended or desired conditions at sample collection. If this archetype is used for representing an ACTION archetype pathway step which correlates with the collection being performed or completed, the context will be reflecting the conditions that existed at sample collection and this may also be copied to the 'Confounding factors' element of the OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result archetype.">
            >
            ["id14"] = <
                text = <"Structured source site">
                description = <"A structured description of the area of the body from where the specimen is collected.">
                comment = <"Utilise the more detailed archetypes to describe structured or more complex anatomical sites, or to support recording the source site at run-time by the application. If the body site has been fully identified in the 'Source site' data element, this SLOT becomes redundant.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.sourceSite">
            >
            ["id16"] = <
                text = <"Collection date/time">
                description = <"The date and time that collection has been ordered to take place or has taken place.">
                comment = <"This datetime will be captured primarily in the INSTRUCTION timing, ACTION time or OBSERVATION times. However, as this is a critical piece of information, it can be useful to also associate it directly with the specimen itself.">
            >
            ["id28"] = <
                text = <"Physical properties">
                description = <"Physical dimensions, mass or non-measurable properties of the specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: Volume, mass, circumference, colour, smell, turbidity. This element can be used to specify the properties of the specimen to be collected, in the context of an INSTRUCTION archetype, or the properties of the specimen which was collected, in the context of an ACTION or OBSERVATION archetype. For example, an INSTRUCTION may request the collection of 20 ml of blood, while the corresponding ACTION records that only 15 ml was collected.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.quantity">
            >
            ["id30"] = <
                text = <"Specimen type">
                description = <"The type of specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: Venous blood, bacterial culture, cytology, or tissue sample. Coding of the specimen type with a terminology is preferred, where possible.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.type">
            >
            ["id35"] = <
                text = <"Date/time received">
                description = <"The date and time that the sample was received at the laboratory.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.receivedTime">
            >
            ["id42"] = <
                text = <"Adequacy for testing">
                description = <"Information about whether the specimen was adequate for testing.">
                comment = <"This element is intended to be used to record a judgement about whether or not the specimen quality was good enough for testing, and whether or not testing has been carried out. Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible.">
            >
            ["id43"] = <
                text = <"Specimen quality issue">
                description = <"A specific quality issue with a specimen.">
                comment = <"Coding of the specimen quality issues with a terminology is preferred, where possible.">
            >
            ["id46"] = <
                text = <"Comment">
                description = <"Additional narrative about the specimen not captured in other fields.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.note">
            >
            ["at53"] = <
                text = <"Haemolysed">
                description = <"The specimen was haemolysed.">
            >
            ["at54"] = <
                text = <"Lipaemic">
                description = <"The specimen was lipaemic.">
            >
            ["at55"] = <
                text = <"Incorrect additive">
                description = <"An incorrect additive such as a transport medium or preservative was added to the specimen.">
            >
            ["at56"] = <
                text = <"Insufficient amount">
                description = <"The available amount of specimen was insufficient to undertake the examination.">
            >
            ["at63"] = <
                text = <"Satisfactory">
                description = <"The specimen is of sufficient quality to allow reporting.">
            >
            ["at64"] = <
                text = <"Unsatisfactory - analysed">
                description = <"The specimen is unsatisfactory but has been analysed.">
            >
            ["at65"] = <
                text = <"Unsatisfactory - not analysed">
                description = <"The specimen is unsatisfactory and has not been analysed.">
            >
            ["id68"] = <
                text = <"Collection setting">
                description = <"Identification of the physical setting in which the specimen is collected.">
                comment = <"For example: laboratory outpatient clinic, at home, or hospital ward. This specifies the type of specimen collection location within the healthcare environment. The specimen collection setting may provide additional information relevant to the analysis of the result.">
            >
            ["id69"] = <
                text = <"Processing details">
                description = <"Structured details about preparation or processing of the specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: Staining or fixation.">
            >
            ["id71"] = <
                text = <"Specimen collector identifier">
                description = <"Identifier of the person or organisation responsible for collecting the specimen.">
                comment = <"This element is intended to be used where the specimen has already been collected and the actual collector is known.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.collector">
            >
            ["id72"] = <
                text = <"Specimen collector details">
                description = <"The person or organisation responsible for collecting the specimen.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.collection.collector">
            >
            ["id80"] = <
                text = <"Collection description">
                description = <"Narrative description about the collection of the specimen.">
            >
            ["id81"] = <
                text = <"Number of containers">
                description = <"The total number of physical units holding this specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: Number of buckets, jars, vials, tubes, blocks, slides or grids.">
            >
            ["id84"] = <
                text = <"Additional details">
                description = <"Additional structured details about the specimen.">
                comment = <"For example: details about needle biopsies in prostate cancer, where both the request and reporting about the specimen are detailed and specific.">
            >
            ["id86"] = <
                text = <"Container details">
                description = <"Details about containers used.">
            >
            ["id88"] = <
                text = <"Source site">
                description = <"Identification of the body site or other location from where the specimen is collected.">
                comment = <"For example: 'wound on left calf', 'IV cannula right arm', 'right kidney'.
Coding of the name of the source site with a terminology is preferred, where possible. Use this data element to record precoordinated source sites. If the requirements for recording the source site are determined at run-time by the application or require more complex modelling such as relative locations then use the 'Structured source site' SLOT in this archetype. If the source site is included in the 'Specimen type' via precoordinated codes, this data element becomes redundant.">
            >
            ["id89"] = <
                text = <"External identifier">
                description = <"A unique identifier of the specimen, assigned by a party external to the laboratory.">
                comment = <"For example: 'Requester ID', 'Archive ID, 'Biobank ID'.">
                fhir_mapping = <"Specimen.identifier">
            >
            ["at90"] = <
                text = <"Icteric">
                description = <"The specimen was icteric.">
            >
            ["at91"] = <
                text = <"Handling error">
                description = <"An error arose when handling the specimen. For example: Incorrect storage, broken container.">
            >
            ["at92"] = <
                text = <"Age">
                description = <"The specimen was too old to analyse or to analyse accurately.">
            >
            ["at93"] = <
                text = <"Technical failure">
                description = <"The specimen could not be analysed for technical reasons.">
            >
            ["id94"] = <
                text = <"Transport details">
                description = <"Structured details about transport of the specimen.">
            >
            ["at95"] = <
                text = <"Clotted">
                description = <"The specimen was clotted.">
            >
            ["at96"] = <
                text = <"Incorrectly labelled">
                description = <"The specimen was labelled incorrectly.">
            >
            ["id97"] = <
                text = <"Digital representation">
                description = <"Structured details about a digital representation of the specimen.">
                comment = <"For example the scanned image of a histopathology slide.">
            >
            ["id98"] = <
                text = <"Specimen description">
                description = <"Narrative description about the specimen being examined.">
                comment = <"For example: the color and viscosity of a liquid; the shape of a solid tissue; or a description of tissue fragments.">
            >
            ["id99"] = <
                text = <"Specimen label">
                description = <"A name or label describing the specimen.">
                comment = <"Usually only relevant for anatomical pathology samples. For example: 'Sigmoid resection with a piece of bladder wall' or 'Aggregate of multiple skin biopsy fragments'.">
            >
            ["id100"] = <
                text = <"Number of fragments">
                description = <"The number of tissue fragments comprising the specimen.">
                comment = <"Usually only relevant when a number of tissue fragments are being examined and reported on as a single specimen.">
            >
            ["id101"] = <
                text = <"Storage details">
                description = <"Structured details about the storage of the specimen.">
            >
            ["ac9000"] = <
                text = <"Specimen quality issue (synthesised)">
                description = <"A specific quality issue with a specimen. (synthesised)">
